From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] VU1 interpreter: per-cycle checks inline; compile-time hazard check for translated pairs

What it is for:
  After patch 0027 the commit pass rarely has work, but it was still
  called on every VU cycle (advanceOneCycle and microAddressMask were out
  of line too), its prologue costing more than its "nothing due" check.
  And the hazard check (calculatePairReadyCycle) and write marking
  (markPairWrites) walked the decoded usage lists at run time even for
  translated pairs, whose lists are compile-time constants.

The change:
  - advanceOneCycle and microAddressMask are inline; advanceOneCycle calls
    commitReadyPipelines only when m_cycle reaches m_nextCommitCycle and
    progressXgkick only while an XGKICK is active (both functions keep
    their own checks).
  - execPairWith takes a timing policy: DynamicTiming (the interpreter)
    calls calculatePairReadyCycle/markPairWrites as before; ConstTiming<D>
    (translated code, D the pair's constexpr decoded form passed as a
    template argument) calls calculatePairReadyCycleConst<D> and
    markPairWritesConst<D>, the same checks and stores unrolled with
    if constexpr (one max per lane read, one store per lane written, in
    the same order).
  - VU1NativeAccess::execPairUpper/execPairUpperLower take the pair as a
    template argument too.
  Same results. Tested: ps2xTest 454/454; the Ben 10 port's 40 captured
  VU1 workloads give the same checksums and cycle count with and without
  its translated code; translated code 291 M -> 214 M instructions.

